  "question": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\qt0061_aa1090505519.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 116px;\"/></p><p>Consider the given reaction. The total number of oxygen atoms present per molecule of the product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is _________.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>During ozonolysis, O<sub>3</sub>​ adds across C=C, and it produces ozonide.</p><p>The ozonide on hydrolysis produces carbonyl compounds. The reaction is used to locate double bond in alkene.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0061_b297b9d04848.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 122px;\"/></p><p>Hence total number of oxygen atom present per molecule of <img src=\"assets\\st0061_947114dd77ee.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 89px;\"/></p><p> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}